  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Think Africa Partnership (TAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Think Africa Partnership (TAP) is a multi-partner fund administered by the World Bank Africa region. Its objectives are to promote economic transformation across Africa by supporting African policy-makers to make better use of evidence and knowledge. The contribution from Norad will support a new work programme called Strategic Partnerships for Private Sector Development and Growth (SP4PG). The African Center for Economic Transformation (ACET) in Ghana will be the key implementing partner.  In 2024, an amendment with explicit focus on women&#x2019;s economic rights and opportunities in selected sub-Saharan African contexts, with project implementation 2024-2026 (Total budget NOK 126 177 000) was added to the agreement. Project implementors for this amendment are Word Bank Group units Africa Gender Innovation Lab (Africa GIL) and Women, Business and the Law (WBL). The 2024-2026 WEE project partnership with Africa GIL and WBL will contribute to TAP 2023 outcome-level pillars 1 (&#x201C;Amplify the knowledge base and support African talent development&#x201D;) and 3 (&#x201C;Building the bridge to policy impact&#x201D;), with a focus to strengthen TAP outcomes with specific targets relating to identification of gender gaps and constraints to women&#x2019;s empowerment in GIL and WBL&#x2019;s advisory and knowledge distribution activities to advance women&#x2019;s economic rights and opportunities in Africa and improve the African knowledge ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
